  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Grey · the 90% floor",
      "items": [
        "UI, networking, files, secrets, installers. These exist with or without an LLM — build them with the craft you already have."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Orange · contamination belt",
      "items": [
        "The sandbox defends against your own agent; the executor eats model-generated strings; config becomes natural language; logs must replay decisions. Old modules, new contracts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Red · the ten percent",
      "items": [
        "A loop that may not stop; context managed like memory with budgets and paging; instructions in natural language; behavior verified only by replay. Nothing in classic software maps to these."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Cyan · old craft, new posting",
      "items": [
        "Gateways, protocol adapters, event stores, kernel reuse: the hard parts are rate limits, failover, and version compatibility — not probability."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Root cause in one sentence",
      "items": [
        "Classic control flow is enumerable; an agent hands the next move to a probabilistic function. The target shifts from 'the interface is correct' to 'safe, recoverable, and observable when misunderstood'."
      ]
    }
  ]
